<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n45580" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">strīdŭlus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj.
		strideo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>creaking</i>, <i>rattling</i>, <i>hissing</i>, <i>whizzing</i>, <i>buzzing</i>, <i>stridulous</i> (<b>poet.</b> and in post-Aug. prose): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">stridula cornus (i. e. hasta),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 12, 267</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fraxinus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Claud. in Ruf. 3, 218</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">plaustra,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					Tr. 3, 12, 30</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fax lacrimoso stridula fumo fuit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. M.
					10, 6</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">manus monstri (i. e. elephanti),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
					9, 627</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">stridula et tenuis vox,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Ep. 56, 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">examina apum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Claud. Cons. Hon. 4, 380</span></i>
			.</div>
